  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given square \\(ABCD\\) with side \\(8\\) feet. A circle is drawn through vertices \\(A\\) and \\(D\\) and tangent to side \\(BC.\\) The radius of the circle, in feet, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(5\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "5"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Place the center at \\((h,4).\\) Since the circle passes through \\(A,\\) \\[ r^2=h^2+16. \\] Tangency to \\(x=8\\) gives \\(r=8-h.\\) Therefore \\(h^2+16=(8-h)^2,\\) so \\(h=3\\) and \\(r=5.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Place \\(A=(0,0),\\) \\(D=(0,8),\\) and \\(BC\\) on the line \\(x=8\\)",
        "The center lies on the perpendicular bisector of \\(AD\\), and its distance to \\(BC\\) equals the radius"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
